From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maago <maago@example.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 04:17:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Type the views that write the response themselves

The CSV export (0017) and the download (0029) write the response
themselves, so they have been func(w, r) views, and did by hand what a
typed view is given: they parsed the id from the path, read the user and
the database from the request, and had no error to return: before
writing, a panic for a 500; after, a panic(http.ErrAbortHandler) to cut
the connection. A view that writes the response itself can be typed: it
takes what a typed view takes, then w and r, and returns an error:

    func ExportBoard(ctx context.Context, u *auth.User, db maago.DB, in ExportIn, w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) error
    func DownloadAttachment(ctx context.Context, u *auth.User, db maago.DB, in DownloadIn, w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) error

- ExportIn and DownloadIn hold the path's id, an int64. A path whose id
  is not a number is a 404, as for any typed view
- The error is answered as a typed view's until the first byte is out:
  sql.ErrNoRows is a 404, any other a 500 that Config.OnError hears.
  After, the 200 and some rows are out: the runtime cuts the connection,
  so a cut file never looks whole, and OnError hears the error (main's
  comment on OnError says so now). So the export returns ExportRows's
  error, and the csv.Writer's, the same way on any page, and abort,
  which logged and cut, is gone. It sets its CSV headers once the first
  page is read: a 500 is no longer a download named board-1.csv
- The download returns maago.ServeMedia's error: a row whose file is
  gone is its 404. The switch 0029 wrote around ServeMedia is gone, and
  TestAttachments moves a file away to see the 404: a view that drops
  ServeMedia's error sends an empty 200
- The URL functions take the In's int64 now: BoardExportURL(b.ID) and
  AttachmentURL(a.ID), with no fmt.Sprint. The test of an id that is not
  a number asks for the path itself, "/boards/abc/posts.csv"

A func(w, r) view stays for what reads the request as it is, such as a
webhook's body; the board has none now.

